## How to read this page

- A layer's "cannot establish" line is not a criticism of its projects. It is the boundary of the question the layer answers. A project that tried to answer every question would answer none of them well.
- Sizes are GitHub stars at the read time, a rough measure of attention, not of quality or adoption. They date quickly; `python3 tools/rederive.py` re-reads every one, and the [claim ledger](claims.html) records when each was read.
- Statuses change. Every status here was read from the body's own page or repository at the time stated.
- The page is generated. Its data file, `data/atlas.toml`, holds every node with its type, link and measurement, so the atlas can be regenerated from any source that emits the same shape.
